'''Scarab Mages''' can be found in the [[Sophanem Dungeon]] and [[Scabaras Dungeon]], and are also fought during the [[Contact!]] and [[Beneath Cursed Sands]] [[quests]]. They attack using [[Magic]], which the attack looks like a swarm of beetles and hits up to 17 [[hitpoints]].

The mages have an unusual [[attack speed]] of 15, attacking every 9 seconds, making [[Prayer#Prayer flicking|prayer flicking]] very easy against them. This somewhat compensates for their high accuracy and max hit.

Though not directly assigned, Scarab mages may be slain as part of a [[Scabarite]] assignment. These monsters respawn at a slower rate compared to the Locust Riders. As they are scabarites, they take increased damage from the [[keris]] and [[keris partisan]].

A light source is required to fight them in the [[Sophanem Dungeon]], but be aware that Scarab mages are able to extinguish a player's [[Light sources|light source]], '''including [[bullseye lantern]]s'''. Bring a [[tinderbox]]! A [[Firemaking cape]], [[bruma torch]], or Kandarin headgear (with any level of the [[Kandarin Diary]] completed) can be used to eliminate the need for a tinderbox. The [[abyssal lantern]] also works as a light source that they cannot extinguish.

